There are now two handlers registered for the exact same route (`GET ${baseUrl}/meta/:type/:name`). MSW matches handlers in order, so the earlier non-cached handler will intercept requests and this new cache-aware handler will never run. Please remove/replace the earlier `getMetaItem` handler (around lines 279–288) and keep a single implementation that supports cache validation.
```suggestion
            // Enhanced Metadata with Cache Support (separate endpoint to avoid route conflicts)
            http.get(`${baseUrl}/meta-cached/:type/:name`, async ({ params, request }) => {
```

`Cache-Control` header formatting is incorrect when `directives` includes `'max-age'` and `maxAge` is also provided. With the current logic this can emit `public, max-age, max-age=3600` (duplicated/invalid). Consider rendering directives that take values (`max-age`, `stale-while-revalidate`, `stale-if-error`) as `name=value` and omitting the bare token when the numeric value is present.
```suggestion
                        const allDirectives = result.cacheControl.directives || [];
                        const hasMaxAge = result.cacheControl.maxAge !== undefined && result.cacheControl.maxAge !== null;
                        const normalizedDirectives = allDirectives.filter(
                            (directive) => !(directive === 'max-age' && hasMaxAge)
                        );
                        if (hasMaxAge) {
                            normalizedDirectives.push(`max-age=${result.cacheControl.maxAge}`);
                        }
                        headers['Cache-Control'] = normalizedDirectives.join(', ');
```
